{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - Lifecycle - User - New Okta User Created",
	"Description": "A new Okta user was created. A user the adversary creates is a durable foothold that survives password resets on the account they originally compromised.\n\nEvent type: user.lifecycle.create\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/sigmahq/sigma/identity/okta/okta_new_user_created/\n- https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/identity/okta/okta_new_user_created.yml\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "9fbf3f0a-2e8e-5ded-a55e-95d7af71bea4",
	"SearchReference": "c74970cd-e9c5-50e3-b7d0-1465bb5010d3"
